## 6. Baselines and alert thresholds

Fixed thresholds are wrong for this environment because distance differs
per node. Use **per-node baselines** computed from the stored data.

| Metric | Baseline | Warn | Alert |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `ms − 2×tcp_ms` (VA processing) | 24 h median per node | > 2 × median | > 3 × median, or > 500 ms absolute |
| `ms` | 24 h median per node | > 2 × median | > 1000 ms absolute (clients start to notice) |
| `tcp_ms` | 24 h median per node | > 2 × median | > 100 ms (something changed in the path) |
| `dns_ms` for WLB name | 24 h median | > 2 × median | > 500 ms |
| `status` | — | `unknown` | anything else that isn't `good` |
| `next_update − this_update` | 10 min | — | changed (someone altered VA config) |
| `responder` for a node | fixed per node | — | changed (new signing cert — check its expiry) |

Rolling median, not mean: one 3-second outlier shouldn't move the baseline.

Alert on **two consecutive** breaches to avoid paging on a single blip; the
5-minute cadence makes that a 10-minute confirmation, which is acceptable.

---

## 7. Reading the patterns

| What the charts show | What it means | Who to call |
| --- | --- | --- |
| One VA's processing time climbs, others flat | that node: HSM session, GC, DB pool, thread exhaustion | PKI team — thread dump + `vtl verify` on that box |
| Both nodes of one site climb together | site-level: that site's HSM pair, DB, or network to the HSM | PKI + HSM team |
| All four climb together | shared: HSM group, or the probe box itself is struggling | check `run_from` box first, then HSM |
| `tcp_ms` climbs, processing flat | network path | network team |
| `dns_ms` climbs, everything else flat | resolver / WLB nameserver | DNS / WLB team |
| WLB name keeps resolving to one node only | WLB has ejected the other, or proximity policy pins you | WLB team |
| WLB name resolves to a node whose processing is high | WLB health check is not catching slowness | WLB team — health check needs an OCSP probe with a response-time ceiling |
| `status` = `timeout` with normal `tcp_ms` | VA accepted the connection and stalled — backend | PKI team, then HSM |
| `status` = `tcp_error` | JBoss down or port blocked | server team |
| `status` = `unauthorized` | no signing key for this CA on that node (key binding disabled / expired) | PKI team |
| `responder` changed on a node | OCSP signing cert rotated | note the new cert's expiry |

